{
    "background_story": "Franco was a professional golfer known for his unorthodox swing, but it was his masterful approach to the dogleg holes that earned him a reputation as one of the most skilled players on the tour. Growing up in the rolling hills of Tuscany, Franco learned to navigate the winding fairways and treacherous doglegs of his home course. He developed a unique ability to read the curves of the land, often leaving his opponents in awe as he expertly navigated the most challenging holes. Franco's crowning achievement came at the prestigious Masters tournament, where he sank a 30-foot putt on the infamous 13th hole, a notoriously tricky dogleg. The crowd erupted as Franco celebrated his birdie, cementing his status as a master of the dogleg.",
